the grayscale bitcoin trust is the  largest bitcoin fund in the world and  what many people don't know is that even  though it has 20 billion dollars in  assets about 640 000 bitcoin or so it  actually is one of the main reasons why  bitcoin's price went from about 10 000  in october of 2020 to about 64 000 in  march of 2021 the reason is because the  public shares of that fund we're trading  at a premium to the amount of bitcoin  that's actually in the fund itself and  so naturally wall street investors and  many sophisticated financial folks  around the world they started to go and  try to arbitrage it take advantage and  exploit that premium well so many people  went ahead and actually were giving  money to grayscale in order to get that  approximately 20 premium or so that  eventually the premium collapsed and now  it's switched into a discount which of  course is a big problem if you're still  holding the shares so if we go ahead and  we take a look here the bitcoin holdings  of the grayscale bitcoin trust  skyrocketed from the second half of 2020  into the beginning of 2021 but once it  went ahead and it switched from a  premium to a discount they shut off all  new inflows and it's pretty much  flatlined since then if we take a look  at the actual premium and discount  graphic what we can see here is that at  one point the grayscale bitcoin trust  was trading at 35 even 40 premium  meaning the public shares were worth 40  more than the bitcoin in the fund but  now it's trading at a 30 discount  meaning that for every one dollar of  bitcoin in the fund the shares traded 70  cents not a good idea now of course the  grayscale team they don't want this to  happen they want to convert the  grayscale bitcoin trust into an etf  they've been lobbying the sec via  applications and conversation to go  ahead and be the first to convert that  20 billion biggest bitcoin fund in the  world into an etf now the sec has  approved etps in the united states but  their bitcoin futures etfs they're not  bitcoin spot etfs and so naturally as  part of the application process to  convert gbtc into an etf the sec asked  for public comments it's been thousands  of people have written in messages but  one of them recently this week has stood  out from everyone else robert whaley who  is the creator of the vix volatility  index back in the early 1990s he put  forward a multi-page letter to the sec  and he basically broke down an argument  that stated if you're willing to go  ahead and put forward and approve  bitcoin futures etfs then you should  definitely approve a bitcoin spot etf as  well his main argument broke down into  three key elements and that's what  ultimately led him to endorse the nyse  arca application the first thing is that  the index on which gbtc is priced on is  virtually a perfect substitute for the  index that underlies the return risk  exposure for the futures based etf that  the commission already approved his  second point is that the bitcoin spot  market is vastly deeper and more liquid  than the bitcoin futures market and  third the product structure is much more  transparent and well designed now here's  the deal i don't know what's gonna  happen and i know that the sec and the  administration there they have concerns  in the market and they haven't approved  a spot etf i also know that grayscale  and many other applicants want to  actually get the bitcoin spot etf into  the market one of the most compelling  data points i think grayscale put  forward is that if their conversion  occurs it will unlock about eight  billion dollars of economic value for  gbtc holders i hold bolt i have  obviously direct exposure to bitcoin i  also have gbtc exposure in a retirement  account and if i take a look at those  two assets it's been better to hold the  bitcoin than gbtc but what's very  interesting to me is that right now gbtc  is still trading at a 30 discount to nav  and so naturally if somebody was to go  in buy the shares and then wait until  the conversion occurs you would think  that the share price would go back up to  equal nav there's a reason why many  people aren't doing this yet obviously  wall street and the financial markets  are full of super sophisticated  intelligent people who are constantly  looking at opportunities like this and  so it makes you think if the smart money  isn't going ahead and buying this asset  if they don't price in the fact that  they think there's going to be  conversion maybe there won't be but  again nobody has a crystal ball and so  naturally this is going to be something  to watch over the next couple of months  grayscale and many other applicants many  other market participants will continue  to lobby the sec to try to go ahead and  get the application approved convert the  largest bitcoin fund in the world into a  spot etf will it happen i'm not sure  leave a comment on this video let me  know what you think and i'll go in and  i'll respond later but one of the things  that i do think is going to be very  interesting is once they approve one  they have to approve many of them and  likely that will lead to a catalyst of  interest in bitcoin bitcoin continues to  perform pretty well given the macro  environment even though it's down a lot  still over the last two years of the  undisciplined monetary and fiscal policy  bitcoin has outperformed stocks bonds  currencies and other commodities so  naturally if that continues into the  future many investors are going to say i  have to get off zero i have to get some  exposure i need to be where the safety  is where the utility is and that's  ultimately what grayscale and many other  spot etf applicants are betting on be  fascinating to watch can't wait to see  what happens
 

